Congratulations!

Here's some tips from what you've written:

1. Get a lower AC - aim for -50 or as close as you can get.  Get a
T-Shirt and small shield and enchant them to +5.  With your spell
skills maxed out you can wear a small shield and still cast at 0%
failure.

2. At XL 30 you have enough skill slots to get Dagger to Expert and max
out all your spell slots.  You have slots left over for secondary
weapons, so don't be afraid to beef up your spellcasting skills.

3. I like to enchant MB.  For me, it provides MR, MC and curse
absorption.  The confuse, stun, probe, and canceling effects are
secondary and mostly useless.

4. Get your armor to +4 or +5.  You can use cursed ?oEA to bring the
+4's to +3 and then try for +5 with a B?oEA.  That's why it is good to
have some unholy water as well as holy water.

5. Get a new pick axe.

6. Do you have any wands of cancellation?  Are you keeping them in a
sack named EMERGENCY with an extra holy water?  Try it.  It will keep
them away from your BoH.  Or learn cancellation and ditch those wands.

7. Keep identified wands of fire in your main inventory at all times
for when you are surprised by a MF or MMF.

8. Keep the magic lamp.  Consider wishing for a marker from your wand.

9. Do you know magic mapping, cancellation, or remove curse? Those are
all great spells, especially Remove Curse cast at Skilled.  How about
teleport away?  It makes the dungeon a lot smaller.

10.  Save those wishes for stuff you absolutely need.  You don't really
*need* gauntlets of dex in my opinion.  Perhaps you will wand a =oSD?
You might end up needing a marker, or candles (you didn't mention
those), or a certain spellbook.  You might wish for a T-shirt if you
can't find one.  Also, if you switch to a SDSM you can ditch the AoR
for an AoLS.  That insurance is nice to have if you are worried about
dying.

As for could you win the game with this setup ... sure, you could.  It
could be better, but an ascension is definitely a possibility even with
what you have.

A couple of other things:

DO NOT TRY TO CONVERT MOLOCHS ALTAR.


*Ahem*

Seriously, don't.  Bad things could happen, like loss of protection or
getting disintegrated (or your stuff getting disintegrated).  Moloch
rejects all your sacrifices.  Even the unicorns.

Also, you lost your protection for a reason.  You did something to
anger your god.  Don't do things that anger your god and it won't
happen again.  You can still ascend without protection, but the extra
AC is nice.

As for the planes, here's what I do.  Bring ?oGD to find the portals.
Earth is a cake walk with /oDig.  Air is pretty easy with =oLev and
=oC.  Use /oDeath or Polymorph on Elemtals that engulf you.  Fire is
pretty easy if you are levitating and your stuff is fireproof, which it
should be at that point.  If you fall in lava, cast Cone of Cold or zap
/oCold down and dig out of the frozen lava.  On water, beware the water
species.  Use /oSDD or the amulet or C?oGD to track the moving portal.
On Astral, tactics vary.  I like to use conflict (so I don't keep the
angel pet) to make battles easier.  Consider dropping the amulet to
bring costing costs down.  Use WoDeath against Famine and Pestilence,
and MM against Death.  Be sure to sac on the right altar.  Use ":" to
check.  Be sure it is the real amulet.  Check by trying to put it in
your bag.  Then win the game.



